---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout 
  title="Terms — Cutline" 
  description="What Cutline is and is not. A public disclaimer for the cut path DNS service."
>
  <h1>Terms</h1>

  <section class="intro">
    <p class="lead">
      This is a plain-language notice about what Cutline is and what it is not. 
      It is not a terms of service. You are not signing a contract.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What Cutline Is</h2>
    <p>
      Cutline is an open-source cut-path DNS resolver. It is operated by Dov Allison as a free public service.
    </p>
    <p>
      The purpose of Cutline is to provide a DNS resolver that does not resolve the <a href="/spec">Narge content class</a>. 
      That is the only purpose. If you do not want the Narge content class to resolve on a device or network, 
      you may point that device or network at this DNS resolver.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What Cutline Is Not</h2>
    <p>
      Cutline is not a business. It is not a product for sale. It is not a warranty. It is not a kids safety service, 
      a compliance service, or a filtering solution beyond the narrow Narge class.
    </p>
    <p>
      There is no company. There is no signup. There is no charge.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Use at Your Own Risk</h2>
    <p>
      You choose to point a device at this resolver. You are responsible for that choice.
    </p>
    <p>
      We do not promise that every Narge name is on the list. We do not promise that every non-Narge name stays up. 
      The list is an approximation. This is an extra path, not a guarantee.
    </p>
    <p>
      We are not responsible for what you can or cannot reach. We are not responsible for other software on your devices. 
      We are not responsible for anyone else's use of the same path.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      Query names are not stored. After a query, the operator cannot look up what you requested. Source IP addresses are 
      kept for 7 days for rate limiting and the public distinct-IP count, then deleted. There is no business model involving 
      your data. For more detail, see the <a href="/privacy">Privacy page</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Open Source</h2>
    <p>
      The resolver configuration, block list sources, and overlay corrections are all public. You can read exactly what is 
      happening and verify it yourself. See the <a href="/spec">Narge specification</a> and the 
      <a href="https://github.com/dov-max/narge-spec" target="_blank" rel="noopener">narge-spec repository</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Feedback</h2>
    <p>
      If you have questions, found a problem, or want to propose a change to the host list, open an issue on 
      <a href="https://github.com/dov-max/narge-spec/issues" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Not Legal Advice</h2>
    <p>
      This page is a notice. It describes what Cutline is and what it is not. It is not legal advice. 
      It does not create rights or obligations beyond what the law already provides.
    </p>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .intro {
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl);
  }

  .lead {
    font-size: 1.25rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  section {
    margin: var(--spacing-2xl) 0;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
  }

  p {
    line-height: 1.7;
  }
</style>
